# SELF-RADIATION: bar_self_radiation on adds each band mode's own radiated power per unit modal velocity, W from the receiver's Burton-Miller solve, as max(W, 0) to the loss row's damping; the loss row is the near-vacuum one, so the air counts once. Without the term the engine refused this tube at the 306 mm column it first carried: the mutual radiation resistance between the tube's fifth mode (2396.6 Hz) and the bar's third vertical mode (2422.9 Hz), -50.9, needs that bar mode to decay at least 0.995 per second against the tube mode's 652, and the near-vacuum loss alone gives it 0.635.
bar_self_radiation	on
